  "highlights": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "value": "<p>Established in 1927, the University of Hull is a public university located in Hull, East Yorkshire, UK. You’ll find it situated on a campus that combines both historic and modern architecture. The university offers a wide range of undergraduate and postgraduate programs across various disciplines, including arts, business, education, health, and sciences.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Student life",
      "value": "<p>The University of Hull provides you with a vibrant community through numerous societies, sports clubs, and support services. You can choose from over 100 student-led societies and approximately 50 sports clubs affiliated with the Athletic Union. The university offers one-to-one academic and English language assistance, ensuring you excel in your studies. Plus, the university provides comprehensive wellness support, including mental health services.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Accommodation",
      "value": "<p>At the University of Hull, you'll find a variety of on-campus accommodation options designed to suit your preferences. The university offers three main halls of residence: Taylor Court, the Courtyard, and Westfield Court.</p><p style=\"text-align:center;\">Additionally, if you’re looking for budget-friendly accommodation options outside the campus, feel free to <a href=\"https://edvoy.com/app/\">download our app</a> and check out the Stays feature!</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Facilities",
      "value": "<p><strong>Library</strong><br>The Brynmor Jones Library is the university's primary library, housing over a million books and digital resources. You can find several study environments, including quiet zones for individual study and collaborative spaces for group work.</p><p><strong>Sports</strong><br>You can always remain active with the state-of-the-art sports facilities at the university, including a 12-court sports hall, a 120-station gym, dedicated fitness studios, floodlit 3G pitches, pitch-side changing rooms, and a new strength and conditioning suite.</p><p><strong>Laboratory</strong><br>The University of Hull offers many specialised laboratory facilities across various disciplines. These include the Biomedical Sciences labs, Marine and Environmental Science facilities, Sport, Health, and Exercise Science labs, and many more.</p><p><strong>Cafeteria</strong><br>You can find various dining options across campus, including the Courtyard Cafe and the Canham Turner Building Cafe. Additionally, the Hull University Union offers catering outlets and a shop, ensuring you have quick food options as well.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    }
  ],
